:R-HSA-199220  a            obo:GO_0015939 , owl:NamedIndividual ;
        rdfs:comment        "Panthothenate (vitamin B5) is the precursor of coenzyme A (Robishaw and Neely 1985) and is the prosthetic group of acyl carrier protein (ACP) (Joshi et al. 2003). Its name is derived from the Greek pantothen meaning \"from everywhere\" and small quantities of pantothenic acid are found in nearly every foodstuff." ;
        rdfs:label          "Vitamin B5 (pantothenate) metabolism" ;
